title The count that stopped at the dollar sign
prompt Keaton -- ratchet the 51
think The 51 was wrong, and so were the 304 before it. Both readings stopped at the dollar sign: the dominant spelling is femit-bin=${bin}, and a Rishi binding is almost always let bin = "lotus/bin/thing" -- a literal tree path wearing a variable's clothes.
think Following let to its value is the whole reason this is a scan rather than a grep. The true reading is 1,853 sites across 1,224 of 1,982 witness files, with exactly SIX penned -- one of them the guard I repaired earlier today.
obs I REPORTED A WRONG NUMBER TO KEATON TWICE BEFORE MEASURING PROPERLY, by roughly 6x and then 36x in the other direction. Both figures stand in the record with the reason, and the control now carries a mutation that breaks the resolution and asserts the count COLLAPSES, so the next reader cannot repeat it silently.
obs A DIALECT GUARD CAUGHT A GNU-ONLY sed -i in my control. GNU takes no argument and BSD requires one, so on the macOS clone the mutation would have failed and its leg passed vacuously -- a plant that plants nothing, REDS %519 in the very control built to prove a plant bites. It calls sed_inplace from tools/fixtures/s/shell_portable.sh now.
obs THE CONTROL CAUGHT A HANG IN MY OWN SCAN. Its empty-tree leg blocked forever, because awk with an empty file list reads STDIN. A scan that hangs on a tree with no witnesses would have hung the roster pass on a fresh clone. Passing /dev/null alongside the list guarantees one file argument.
obs Hand-verified one counted site rather than trusting the aggregate: tools/z/zhang_suen_witness.rish binds image/bin/zhang_suen and emits to it, and image/bin is a gitignored build directory. Correctly classified.
obs THE CEILING IS SET AT THE TRUE READING rather than at an aspiration, and only falls. A gate that reds on ordinary work is one somebody turns off, and this backlog was not made today.
obs The roster reads roster_broken for a PRE-EXISTING reason rather than mine: every structural reading of my addition is zero, and the verdict comes from two recorded reds. remember_git_nib runs GREEN now; stash_record is REDS %636, open and waiting on Keaton's word.
